# Upload filter for `gcloud builds submit` (scripts/deploy-api.sh). Without this file gcloud silently derives
# one from .gitignore, which is not the Docker context.
#
# gitignore SYNTAX, not Docker's: a pattern without a leading slash matches at ANY depth, so `lib/` would also
# drop apps/api/src/lib (it did, 2026-10-22 — the API image could not find ./lib/session-token). Root-only
# entries are therefore anchored with a leading slash. Do not `#!include:.dockerignore` — Docker's root-anchored
# patterns mean something else here.
#
# Cloud Build in this repo builds the API image only (the web app deploys via Vercel), so the web app's art
# and sources stay home too: the first upload carried 48 MiB of them and timed out.
node_modules/
.git/
.env
.env.*
/lib/
/contracts/
/docs/
/test/
*.md
.claude/
.github/
/design/
/packages/battle-engine/
.next/
/apps/web/out/
/apps/web/public/
/apps/web/src/
/apps/web/*.css
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage/
/out/
/cache/
/broadcast/
/deployments/
/audio-masters/
/scripts/harness/out/
/scripts/harness/chrome-profile/
/scripts/harness/chrome.log
/scripts/harness/*.out
/scripts/e2e/.runs/
.vercel/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
